BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Purple Fringeless Orchid Stroll
DTSTART:20260723T180000
DTEND:20260723T193000
UID:7e4221c59831e145b2e9f2cd0a3ca6d3@sycamorelandtrust.org
DESCRIPTION:Did you know that Indiana is home to more than 40 species of o
 rchids? At Beanblossom Bottoms Nature Preserve\, we&#8217\;ll search for t
 he striking purple fringeless orchid in bloom. This tall\, showy native or
 chid thrives in the preserve’s sunny\, poorly-drained floodplain wetland
 s and seasonal swales\, where spring flooding and open conditions create i
 deal habitat. While the species is considered globally secure\, it is rare
  or imperiled in many states and appears on Indiana’s state watch list\,
  making local populations especially important to protect! Take a stroll w
 ith us as we revel in the beauty of this plant!
LOCATION:Beanblossom Bottoms Nature Preserve
URL:https://sycamorelandtrust.org/2026/07/purple-fringeless-orchid-stroll/
X-SOURCE:Sycamore Land Trust
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mysterious Moths with Jeanette Jaskula
DTSTART:20260724T203000
DTEND:20260724T230000
UID:544a7c533ef1b4a071fa0a77c958965f@sycamorelandtrust.org
DESCRIPTION:As darkness falls over Beanblossom Bottoms Nature Preserve\, t
 he mysterious world of moths comes to life. Join naturalist and moth enthu
 siast Jeanette Jaskula for an evening where science and wonder come togeth
 er as we use specialized lights and lures to attract an incredible diversi
 ty of moths. Through close observation and discussion\, we&#8217\;ll explo
 re moths&#8217\; fascinating life cycles\, remarkable adaptations\, ecolog
 ical importance\, and the surprising roles they play as pollinators and fo
 od for other wildlife.
LOCATION:Beanblossom Bottoms Nature Preserve
URL:https://sycamorelandtrust.org/2026/07/mysterious-moths-with-jeanette-j
 askula/
X-SOURCE:Sycamore Land Trust
END:VEVENT
